    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25356" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jūnĭus</span></b> , a,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>name of a
			Roman</i> gens: e. g. M. and D. Junius Brutus.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jūnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., Junian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">familia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					3, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 2,
					5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lex,</span>”
				<i>proposed by Junius</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 2, 9, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 16, 5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mensis,</span>”
				<i>the sixth month, June</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 6, 2, 6</span></i>
			. —Esp., as <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jūnĭus</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Att. 5, 21, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 6, 88</span></i>.</div>
